<BaseLayout
  title="Authors"
  description="The editorial team behind Sourcedreviews — Kitchen, Home & Garden, Tech, and Gift categories."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <header>
      <h1>Authors</h1>
      <p class="summary">The editorial team behind Sourcedreviews. Each section is curated by an editor with a specialty, drawing on independent published testing and aggregated verified-buyer feedback.</p>
    </header>

    <h2 id="daniel-reeves">Daniel Reeves — Editor in Chief</h2>
    <p>Daniel has been writing about consumer products since 2019. He founded Sourcedreviews and curates the cross-category coverage. He draws on published testing from independent labs, manufacturer specifications, and aggregated verified-buyer feedback to produce every article on this site.</p>
    <p>Daniel does not perform hands-on testing of every product reviewed on this site; for the full editorial process, see <a href="/our-method/">Our Method</a>.</p>
    <p>Daniel can be reached at <a href="mailto:contact@sourcedreviews.com">contact@sourcedreviews.com</a> for editorial inquiries, corrections, and takedown requests.</p>

    <h2 id="ethan-carter">Ethan Carter — Kitchen and Home & Garden Editor</h2>
    <p>Ethan covers the Kitchen and Home & Garden categories on Sourcedreviews, with a focus on cookware, small appliances, indoor climate, and cleaning equipment. He draws on published testing from America's Test Kitchen, Serious Eats, Good Housekeeping, The Spruce Eats, and Wirecutter / NYT, supplemented by aggregated Amazon verified-buyer feedback.</p>
    <p>Before joining Sourcedreviews, Ethan spent four years writing product coverage for a regional home-and-kitchen trade publication. He does not perform hands-on testing of every product reviewed; see <a href="/our-method/">Our Method</a> for the editorial process.</p>

    <h2 id="ryan-mitchell">Ryan Mitchell — Tech Editor</h2>
    <p>Ryan covers the Tech category on Sourcedreviews, including mechanical keyboards, standing desks, gaming chairs, computer peripherals, and consumer audio. He draws on published testing from Wirecutter / NYT, RTINGS, Tom's Guide, and PCMag, supplemented by aggregated Amazon and direct-to-consumer verified-buyer feedback.</p>
    <p>Before joining Sourcedreviews, Ryan spent three years writing consumer-tech coverage for a specialty retail publication. He does not perform hands-on testing of every product reviewed; see <a href="/our-method/">Our Method</a> for the editorial process.</p>

    <hr />
    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-muted);">
      All editors follow the same <a href="/our-method/">editorial method</a> and the same <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>. We did not perform hands-on testing of any product we recommend.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>